1 Overview
**********

‘rl’ is the command-line interface for the rl programming language.  It
provides tools for running, checking, compiling, packaging, and
generating documentation for rl source files.

   If no command is given and stdin is a terminal, the interactive REPL
is started.


File: rl.info.out,  Node: Commands,  Next: run Command,  Prev: Overview,  Up: Top

2 Commands
**********

‘rl run FILE [-c CODE] [--vm] [--cranelift] [-- ARGS...]’
     Lex, parse, and evaluate a ‘.rl’ source file.

‘rl dev [--vm] [--cranelift]’
     Run the current project by reading ‘rl.toml’.

‘rl new NAME [--no-git] [--script]’
     Scaffold a new project directory or create a standalone script.

‘rl check FILE’
     Type-check a ‘.rl’ file and report errors without running it.

‘rl format FILE’
     Format a ‘.rl’ source file in place.

‘rl compile FILE [-o OUTPUT]’
     Lex, parse, resolve, and compile a ‘.rl’ source file to ‘.rlc’
     bytecode.

‘rl print FILE (-t | -p | -a)’
     Print debug information for a ‘.rl’ source file.

‘rl transpile FILE [-o OUTPUT] [--runtime] [-c] [--opt LEVEL] [-- CC-FLAGS]’
     Transpile a ‘.rl’ source file to C99.

‘rl package FILE [-o OUTPUT] [--vm]’
     Package a ‘.rl’ file into a self-contained binary.

‘rl repl’
     Start the interactive TUI REPL.

‘rl lsp’
     Start the Language Server Protocol server.

‘rl docs TOPIC [--tui] [--website] [--json] [--stdlib] [--concept] [--tutorial]’
     Print language reference and stdlib documentation.

‘rl workflows --check | --package’
     Scaffold GitHub Actions workflow files.


