3 run Command
*************

‘rl run FILE’ lexes, parses, and evaluates a ‘.rl’ source file.
Arguments after the file path are passed to the script as its ‘argv’
array.

3.1 Options
===========

‘-c CODE, --code CODE’
     Execute inline rl code instead of a file.

‘--vm’
     Run through the bytecode VM. This is the default backend.

‘--cranelift’
     JIT compile via cranelift.  Requires the ‘--cranelift’ feature.

3.2 Examples
============

     $ rl run hello.rl
     $ rl run script.rl -- --verbose input.txt
     $ rl run -c 'println("hello")'


