5 new Command
*************

‘rl new NAME’ scaffolds a new project directory with the standard
structure and a ‘rl.toml’ configuration file.  Alternatively, with the
‘--script’ flag, it creates a single standalone ‘.rl’ file.

5.1 Options
===========

‘--no-git’
     Skip running ‘git init’ in the new project directory.

‘--script’
     Create a standalone ‘.rl’ script instead of a project directory.

5.2 Examples
============

     $ rl new my_project
     $ rl new --script my_script


