10 transpile Command
********************

‘rl transpile FILE’ lexes, parses, resolves, type-checks, and transpiles
a ‘.rl’ source file to C99 source code.

10.1 Options
============

‘-o PATH, --output PATH’
     Output ‘.c’ path.  Defaults to FILE with its extension changed to
     ‘.c’.

‘--runtime’
     Also emit ‘rl_runtime.h’ and ‘rl_runtime.c’ alongside the
     transpiled output.

‘-c, --compile’
     After transpiling, invoke ‘cc’ to compile the ‘.c’ file.

‘--opt LEVEL’
     Optimization level forwarded to ‘cc’.  Accepted values: ‘O0’, ‘O1’,
     ‘O2’, ‘O3’, ‘Os’, ‘Og’.  Defaults to ‘O2’ when ‘--compile’ is used.

‘-- CC-FLAGS’
     Extra flags forwarded directly to ‘cc’.

10.2 Examples
=============

     $ rl transpile script.rl
     $ rl transpile script.rl --runtime --compile
     $ rl transpile script.rl --runtime --compile -o output
     $ rl transpile script.rl --runtime --compile -O3 -- -lm


