14 docs Command
***************

‘rl docs TOPIC’ searches names across all documentation categories and
prints the matching entry.  With no TOPIC, it prints everything.  Use
the ‘--tui’ flag for an interactive terminal browser.

14.1 Options
============

‘--tui’
     Browse docs in an interactive terminal UI.

‘--website’
     Open docs in a web browser.

‘--json’
     Print output as JSON instead of Markdown.

‘--stdlib’
     Restrict search to stdlib docs.

‘--concept’
     Restrict search to concept docs.

‘--tutorial’
     Restrict search to tutorial docs.

‘--out-file PATH’
     Write output to a file instead of stdout.

‘--generate’
     Generate documentation for the current project.

‘--html’
     Emit an HTML version of the generated site (used with
     ‘--generate’).

‘--out-dir PATH’
     Output directory for ‘--generate’.

14.2 Examples
=============

     $ rl docs
     $ rl docs map
     $ rl docs --tui
     $ rl docs --stdlib --json
     $ rl docs --generate --html --out-dir site/


